":"activity","detail":"A narrow medieval stair ends on a deck above Piata Mare, looking across the tiled roofs and their eyebrow windows.","link":"https://turism.sibiu.ro/en/","evidence":{"n_sources":8,"of":12,"urls":["https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Sibiu","https://www.romaniatourism.com/sibiu.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sibiu","https://www.europeanbestdestinations.com/destinations/sibiu/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Driving the Transfagarasan to Balea Lake","type":"activity","detail":"The high road south of the city switchbacks to a glacial lake near two thousand metres, and shuts once the snow arrives.","season":[7,8,9,10],"evidence":{"n_sources":7,"of":12,"urls":["https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Sibiu","https://wikitravel.org/en/Sibiu","https://www.romaniatourism.com/sibiu.html","https://www.europeanbestdestinations.com/destinations/sibiu/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"The two squares and the Bridge of Lies","type":"activity","detail":"Piata Mare and Piata Mica sit one behind the other under the Council Tower, joined by the first cast iron bridge in the country. The eyelid dormers in the roofs around them are why the town looks like it is watching you.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":12,"urls":["https://www.mywanderlust.pl/things-to-do-in-sibiu-romania/","https://kristatheexplorer.com/post/best-things-to-do-in-sibiu-romania/","https://romaniatourism.com/sibiu.html"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Hiking the Cindrel and Fagaras mountains","type":"trail","detail":"Marked routes start above Paltinis and Rasinari, with the higher Fagaras ridges an hour further out for longer days.","season":[6,7,8,9],"evidence":{"n_sources":5,"of":12,"urls":["https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Sibiu","https://wikitravel.org/en/Sibiu","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sibiu","https://www.europeanbestdestinations.com/destinations/sibiu/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Fortified Saxon churches at Biertan and Valea Viilor","typ